{
  "timeline": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 212,
      "bones": [],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "The skull is not one bone. Most cranial bones meet at sutures. Foramina and fissures provide routes for nerves and vessels.",
      "mode": "intro",
      "camDir": [
        -0.55,
        0.39,
        0.74
      ],
      "lookAt": [
        0,
        0,
        0
      ],
      "dist": 6.5,
      "points": []
    },
    {
      "id": "coronal",
      "start": 212,
      "end": 433,
      "bones": [],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "The coronal suture joins the frontal bone to the two parietal bones. It runs across the top of the skull. Its junction with the sagittal suture is the bregma.",
      "mode": "suture",
      "camDir": [
        0.2,
        0.7,
        0.7
      ],
      "lookAt": [
        0,
        1.0,
        0.3
      ],
      "dist": 4.2,
      "points": [
        {
          "x": 0.59,
          "y": 1.12,
          "z": 0.32,
          "label": "Coronal suture",
          "latin": "Sutura coronalis"
        },
        {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 1.2,
          "z": 0.2,
          "label": "Bregma",
          "latin": "Bregma"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sagittal",
      "start": 433,
      "end": 681,
      "bones": [],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "The sagittal suture runs along the midline between the parietal bones. It meets the coronal suture at the bregma, and the lambdoid suture at the lambda.",
      "mode": "suture",
      "camDir": [
        0,
        1,
        0.3
      ],
      "lookAt": [
        0,
        1.0,
        -0.3
      ],
      "dist": 4.5,
      "points": [
        {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 1.2,
          "z": -0.3,
          "label": "Sagittal suture",
          "latin": "Sutura sagittalis"
        },
        {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 1.2,
          "z": 0.2,
          "label": "Bregma",
          "latin": "Bregma"
        },
        {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 1.1,
          "z": -0.9,
          "label": "Lambda",
          "latin": "Lambda"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lambdoid",
      "start": 681,
      "end": 936,
      "bones": [],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "The lambdoid suture joins the parietal bones to the occipital bone. It runs across the posterior skull. Its junction with the sagittal suture is the lambda.",
      "mode": "suture",
      "camDir": [
        0,
        0.6,
        -0.8
      ],
      "lookAt": [
        0,
        0.7,
        -1.0
      ],
      "dist": 4.2,
      "points": [
        {
          "x": 0.5,
          "y": 0.8,
          "z": -1.0,
          "label": "Lambdoid suture",
          "latin": "Sutura lambdoidea"
        },
        {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 1.1,
          "z": -0.9,
          "label": "Lambda",
          "latin": "Lambda"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "squamous",
      "start": 936,
      "end": 1187,
      "bones": [],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "The squamous suture joins the parietal and temporal bones on each side. Its name refers to their overlapping, scale-like edges.",
      "mode": "suture",
      "camDir": [
        -1,
        0.3,
        0.1
      ],
      "lookAt": [
        -0.9,
        0.3,
