      "camDir": [
        0,
        1,
        0.3
      ],
      "lookAt": [
        0,
        -0.1,
        0.1
      ],
      "dist": 5.0,
      "points": [
        {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -0.05,
          "z": 0.65,
          "label": "Anterior cranial fossa",
          "latin": "Fossa cranii anterior"
        },
        {
          "x": 0.45,
          "y": -0.15,
          "z": 0.05,
          "label": "Middle cranial fossa",
          "latin": "Fossa cranii media"
        },
        {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -0.25,
          "z": -0.55,
          "label": "Posterior cranial fossa",
          "latin": "Fossa cranii posterior"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cribriform",
      "start": 1784,
      "end": 2137,
      "bones": [
        1,
        2,
        3
      ],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "The cribriform plate of the ethmoid forms part of the nasal roof. Olfactory nerve filaments pass through its small openings. A fracture may cause loss of smell or a cerebrospinal fluid leak from the nose.",
      "mode": "vault",
      "camDir": [
        0,
        1,
        0.25
      ],
      "lookAt": [
        0,
        0.0,
        0.69
      ],
      "dist": 3.0,
      "points": [
        {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0.05,
          "z": 0.69,
          "label": "Cribriform plate",
          "latin": "Lamina cribrosa"
        },
        {
          "x": 0.12,
          "y": 0.05,
          "z": 0.75,
          "label": "Olfactory filaments",
          "latin": "Fila olfactoria (CN I)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "optic-canal",
      "start": 2137,
      "end": 2386,
      "bones": [
        1,
        2,
        3
      ],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "The optic canal lies in the lesser wing of the sphenoid. It transmits the optic nerve and ophthalmic artery. The optic nerve carries visual signals from the retina toward the brain.",
      "mode": "vault",
      "camDir": [
        0.2,
        1,
        0.4
      ],
      "lookAt": [
        0.2,
        0.0,
        0.52
      ],
      "dist": 3.0,
      "points": [
        {
          "x": 0.2,
          "y": 0.02,
          "z": 0.52,
          "label": "Optic canal",
          "latin": "Canalis opticus"
        },
        {
          "x": 0.3,
          "y": 0.0,
          "z": 0.55,
          "label": "Optic nerve (CN II)",
          "latin": "N. opticus"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sof",
      "start": 2386,
      "end": 2686,
      "bones": [
        1,
        2,
        3
      ],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "The superior orbital fissure lies between the sphenoid wings. It transmits cranial nerves three, four, and six, the ophthalmic division of nerve five, and the superior ophthalmic vein.",
