          "x": 0.35,
          "y": -0.05,
          "z": 0.45,
          "label": "Superior orbital fissure",
          "latin": "Fissura orbitalis superior"
        },
        {
          "x": 0.45,
          "y": -0.05,
          "z": 0.4,
          "label": "CN III, IV, V1, VI",
          "latin": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sphenoid-trio",
      "start": 2686,
      "end": 3086,
      "bones": [
        1,
        2,
        3
      ],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "Three important openings in the greater wing of the sphenoid. The foramen rotundum transmits the maxillary nerve, the second trigeminal division. The foramen ovale transmits the mandibular division. The foramen spinosum transmits the middle meningeal artery. These markers are schematic.",
      "mode": "vault",
      "camDir": [
        0.2,
        1,
        0.25
      ],
      "lookAt": [
        0.4,
        0.0,
        0.1
      ],
      "dist": 3.5,
      "points": [
        {
          "x": 0.25,
          "y": 0.05,
          "z": 0.3,
          "label": "Foramen rotundum",
          "latin": "N. maxillaris (V2)"
        },
        {
          "x": 0.32,
          "y": 0.02,
          "z": 0.15,
          "label": "Foramen ovale",
          "latin": "N. mandibularis (V3)"
        },
        {
          "x": 0.4,
          "y": 0.0,
          "z": 0.1,
          "label": "Foramen spinosum",
          "latin": "A. meningea media"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "iam",
      "start": 3086,
      "end": 3456,
      "bones": [
        1,
        2,
        3,
        6
      ],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "The internal acoustic meatus opens on the petrous temporal bone. It carries the facial and vestibulocochlear nerves and the labyrinthine artery. The facial nerve continues into the facial canal. Temporal bone trauma may cause facial weakness, hearing loss, or vertigo.",
      "mode": "vault",
      "camDir": [
        0.85,
        0.35,
        -0.3
      ],
      "lookAt": [
        0.34,
        -0.25,
        -0.16
      ],
      "dist": 3.5,
      "points": [
        {
          "x": 0.34,
          "y": -0.25,
          "z": -0.16,
          "label": "Internal acoustic meatus",
          "latin": "Meatus acusticus internus"
        },
        {
          "x": 0.38,
          "y": -0.2,
          "z": -0.12,
          "label": "CN VII, VIII",
          "latin": "N. facialis, N. vestibulocochlearis"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "posterior-base",
      "start": 3456,
      "end": 3872,
      "bones": [],
      "labels": [],
      "text": "The foramen magnum transmits the brainstem continuing as the spinal cord, the vertebral arteries, and spinal roots of the accessory nerve. The jugular foramen carries nerves nine, ten, and eleven and venous drainage. The hypoglossal canal transmits the twelfth nerve.",
      "mode": "below",
